Kind: widen
Issue: #624
Holds open: the two loads of a current_thread() without #646's fix, in mutex_lock_assert_safe(), for delay(160), what 1000 pause instructions lasted at OMEGA's maximum clock -- a time and not a count, which under TCG lasts as many times longer as the host is slower (about 1 ms at 1.4 GHz) -- so a preemption and a move between them is likely, and the fixed tree, one load after the same wait, must still pass
Run: --entry 22 1200 -smp 4

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/lock.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/lock.c
index 1f10039a..fb332bb8 100644
--- a/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/lock.c
+++ b/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/lock.c
@@ -2143,11 +2143,49 @@ etap_mutex_unlock(
  * means the first read named another processor's thread, as the two loads
  * of #646 could.  The passing path reads the thread and its event once each.
  */
+#if	MACH_ASSERT
+/*
+ * ablations/624-widen.patch: the two loads of a current_thread() without
+ * #646's fix, held apart in the check #624 saw fail, so that a preemption and
+ * a move between them is likely rather than rare.  With the fix there is one
+ * load, and the same wait before it opens no window.  The wait is delay()'s,
+ * a time and not a count of pause instructions: under TCG every pause leaves
+ * the translated code, so a count lasts as many times longer as the host is
+ * slower, and with 1000 of them a boot of entry 22 took 29 minutes at 1.4 GHz
+ * against 22 seconds without.  Until the TSC is calibrated there is no wait:
+ * this check runs from the first mutex, and delay() has nothing to count on
+ * before the rulers are found.
+ */
+#ifdef	__x86_64__
+#include <x86_64/time/tsc.h>
+#endif
+
+#define	WIDEN_624_US	160
+
+static thread_t
+widen_624_current_thread(void)
+{
+#if	!defined(__x86_64__)
+	return current_thread();	/* entry 22 is x86-64's; i386 only builds */
+#elif	MACHINE_CURRENT_THREAD && !defined(CURRENT_THREAD_TWO_LOADS)
+	if (tsc_hz() != 0)
+		delay(WIDEN_624_US);
+	return current_thread();
+#else
+	int		cpu = cpu_number_hint();	/* see 646-two-loads.patch */
+
+	if (tsc_hz() != 0)
+		delay(WIDEN_624_US);
+	return cpu_data[cpu].active_thread;
+#endif
+}
+#endif	/* MACH_ASSERT */
+
 void
 mutex_lock_assert_safe(void)
 {
 #if	MACH_ASSERT
-	thread_t	self = current_thread();
+	thread_t	self = widen_624_current_thread();
 	thread_t	again;
 	event_t		event;
 
